+/*
+ * esparser_drain_work() - push the tail AUs of a stream into the ESPARSER
+ *
+ * V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP cannot do this inline: the client is usually
+ * single-threaded, so while it sits in the STOP ioctl it cannot recycle
+ * capture buffers into the m2m queue. Feeding the remaining AUs needs those
+ * buffers, so the ioctl would be waiting for userspace to make progress
+ * that userspace can only make once the ioctl returns. Running the flush
+ * from a delayed work lets the client drain concurrently and the buffers
+ * do come back.
